Addendum; from quaffing. Dipping will dry it up just fine.

Dipping also lets you check for wishes without the possibility of the
inventory-cursing effect. Once you can handle snakes, nymphs and demons,
dipping an object you would like uncursed (or one you don't mind being
cursed) is the way to squeeze the remaining utility out of confirmed
non-magical fountains. Since there is also a reduced chance of drying the
fountain up, this slightly increases the expected yield of wishes.
